
  <sn><md>### Undo in Git

A Complete Guide to Reversing Changes

Git provides several ways to undo changes. The correct command depends on **where the change currently exists**: in the working directory, staging area, local commits, or the remote repository.

The most important rule is:

&gt; **Before using an undo command, identify whether the change is in the working tree, staging area, local history, or remote history.**

</md></sn>
